 "unreadable": [],
 "notes": "Cols 83-90 conclude mother-tongue Korku (subsidiaries Hindustani, Marathi, Gondi, Telugu); cols 91-96 mother-tongue Kharia. End of Table XV Part II. Page foot carries the end of the Korwa/Korku footnote begun on p. 366 (see leaf 376). Row 8 Hindustani females '436': final 6 has a broken top but reads 436 (= Korku MT females on leaf 376). Kharia MT totals agree with Part I for every district/state. PRINT INCONSISTENCIES kept as printed: (1) row 57 Chikhli: Korku-Hindustani 124/124 and Korku-Marathi 271/263 printed on the Chikhli line, but leaf 376 prints Chikhli Korku MT nil and Jalgaon (row 58) 653/653 - the subsidiary figures almost certainly belong to Jalgaon (or leaf 376 is a row off). (2) row 41 Raipur (excluding 5 Zamindaris): Kharia MT females printed 16 (confirmed by Part I), but Kharia-Hindustani females printed 26 (> 16); both figures clearly printed."
